# Implementation Plan - Fix InitialLoader Import Error

The user is encountering a "Cannot find module" error for `@/components/ui/InitialLoader`. Despite the file existing and the alias being configured, the error persists. This plan aims to resolve the issue by ensuring the component is correctly defined and resolved.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component UI]
#### [MODIFY] [InitialLoader.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/ui/InitialLoader.tsx)
- Add `import React from 'react';` to ensure `React.ReactNode` is correctly typed, as some environments require it even with the new JSX transform.

#### [MODIFY] [layout.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/app/layout.tsx)
- If the above doesn't work, temporarily switch to a relative import to verify if the issue is with the `@/` path alias resolution.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `npx tsc --noEmit` to check for TypeScript errors.
- Check the output of `npm run dev` to see if the error persists in the console/overlay.

### Manual Verification
- Verify that the loading screen appears and then fades out as expected when the app starts.
